==========================================
NETWORKING DAY 03 NOTES — curl & wget
Date: 01-10-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- curl prints the response to the terminal by default; wget saves it to a file by default
- curl -I gets headers only - the fastest way to check if a site is up and what status it returns
- curl -v shows the FULL process: DNS lookup, TCP connect, TLS handshake, then the request/response
- curl -L follows redirects; without it, a redirect just shows as a 301/302 with no body
- curl -s https://api.ipify.org is a quick way to find your public-facing IP address
- wget is better suited to straightforward file downloads (progress bar, resumable with -c)

COMMANDS YOU PRACTICED:
[ ] curl <url>  /  curl -I <url>
[ ] curl -v <url>
[ ] curl -L <url>
[ ] curl -o <file> <url>
[ ] curl -s https://api.ipify.org
[ ] wget <url> -O <file>

paste your real output here :
$ curl -I https://example.com
> 

$ curl -s https://api.ipify.org
> 

$ wget https://example.com -O test.html
> 


